accTitle: Perception and grounding action boundary
accDescr: Perception actions read a snapshot through a read port and return observations with entity, evidence, provenance and source version. Grounding actions accept a typed write request, check its expected snapshot version and action requirements, translate it into a simulation command and pass it to the simulation-world port.
flowchart TB
    Agent[Agent decision procedure]
    subgraph ReadPath[Read-only perception path]
      ReadRequest[Read request]
      Perception[Perception action handler]
      ReadPort[Perception port]
      Snapshot[Current snapshot]
      Observation[Observation with provenance and version]
      ReadRequest --> Perception --> ReadPort --> Snapshot --> Observation
    end
    subgraph WritePath[State-changing grounding path]
      WriteRequest[Typed write request]
      Handler[Grounding action handler]
      Preconditions[Capability and version preconditions]
      Command[Typed simulation command]
      World[Simulation-world port]
      Transition[Simulated transition]
      WriteRequest --> Handler --> Preconditions --> Command --> World --> Transition
    end
    Agent --> ReadRequest
    Observation --> Agent
    Agent --> WriteRequest
    Transition --> Agent
